{title: Whipping Post}

{start_of_bridge: Intro}
[A5]  [Asus4]  [Am]     [*x8]
{end_of_bridge}


{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
              Am   D6/9     Am7  D6/9     G    Am
I've been run down,              and I've been lied to,
G     Am         D6/9      Am7       D6/9       G    Am
And I don't know why I let that mean woman make me a fool
D6/9         G  Am    D6/9    Am7  D6/9       G   Am
She took all my money,             wrecked my new car
Am             D6/9      Am7       D6/9    G
Now she's with one of my good time buddies
Am               D6/9       Am7
Drinkin' in some cross town bar
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus}
{comment: D7    **          E7}
Sometimes I feel, sometimes I feel,
Like I've been [A]tied to the [D7]whippin' post[D7/C]
[A]Tied to the [D7]whippin' post,[D7/C]
[A]Tied to the [D7]whippin' post,[D7/C]
[C]   [*N.C.]Good lord, I feel like I'm dying
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_bridge: Instrumental}
